  22:     """
  23:     Build a compact square of concentric layers, coloring layers by foreground segment length from longest outside to shortest inside.
  24: 
  25:     Input structure
  26:     - The background is the dominant color.
  27:     - Each foreground object is a monochrome 4-connected straight horizontal or vertical segment.
  28:     - Segment lengths are distinct, and their descending order gives the outside-to-inside layer order.
  29: 
  30:     Rule
  31:     - Let N be the length of the longest segment, and create an N x N output grid.
  32:     - Sort the segments by decreasing length.
  33:     - Fill the outermost square layer with the longest segment's color, then each next inner layer with the next segment's color.
  34: 
  35:     Key insight
  36:     - The input positions and orientations of the segments are irrelevant; their lengths are an ordered legend for the concentric output layers.
  37:     """
  38:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  39:     bg = get_bg(g)
  40:     components = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True)
